Log-scale spectrogram ruler ticks

The spectrogram ruler showed only a few labels (e.g. 20Hz, 5000Hz, 20kHz)
on a logarithmic scale, worst on short multi-view channels. Two causes:

- shared::axisTicks() used linear steps (every 5000 Hz) for every scale,
  so on a log axis the ticks bunched up near the top. Log scale now ticks
  at m * 10^n: majors at 1, 2, 5; minors at the other digits. Ranges
  narrower than a decade still use linear steps, which are denser there.
- removeOverlappingTicks() dropped a label if it was close to either
  neighbor, even neighbors that were themselves dropped, so dense tick
  sets lost almost every label. It now keeps the end labels, then
  places the rest roundest value first (1, 5, 2 x 10^n), checking only
  against labels already kept. End labels get an extra half label of
  clearance because the ruler pins them inside the axis.

Includes unit tests in src/shared/tests/axisticks_tests.cpp.

Apply against an Audacity 4.x tree:
  git apply 0004-log-scale-spectrogram-ruler-ticks.patch

